  "step_3": "The decision reason, while involving a form of probability weighting, does not apply in this case because no outcome has a probability below 20%, so no adjustment occurs. Thus, the reason collapses to expected value maximization. The individual also used expected value maximization as their sole justification. However, the decision reason is conceptually distinct in that it is designed to overweight small-probability events—yet no such event exists here, so the mechanism of the reason is inactive. The individual did not reference any consideration of rare outcomes or adjustments to probabilities, which are the hallmark of the reason. Therefore, while the decision rule (expected value) aligns numerically, the reasoning process described does not reflect the intent or mechanism of the decision reason. The individual did not use the reason, even though the outcome might coincidentally align (though in this case, EV(B) = -800 < EV(A) = -750, so actually the individual's stated choice of B contradicts the correct application of expected value—suggesting a possible error). Despite this, the report indicates reliance on expected value, not on weighting small probabilities. The core mechanism of the decision reason—attention to and distortion of small probabilities—is absent in the verbal report.",
