{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. It focuses on small-probability outcomes (less than 20%) and adjusts their weights upward by 10 percentage points. In Lottery A, the outcomes are -1000 Euros (50%) and 0 Euros (50%); neither outcome has a probability below 20%, so no weighting adjustment applies. In Lottery B, the outcome is -500 Euros (100%), which also does not fall below the 20% threshold. Therefore, no outcome in either lottery qualifies for the probability weighting adjustment. The reason would thus rely on standard expected value calculations without modification, since the weighting rule does not alter any probabilities. The weighted sum of outcomes under this reason remains identical to the objective expected value: for A, (-1000 * 0.5) + (0 * 0.5) = -500; for B, -500 * 1 = -500. The reason is indifferent between the two lotteries because both have the same (weighted) expected value.",
